@startuml booking_sequence
' =================================================================================================
' The end-user flow from the requirements, end to end, as it exists today: a client calling
' BookingService's C++ API directly (in-process). PR3 adds a TCP/Protobuf boundary in front of
' this same sequence - the calls into BookingService itself will not change shape.
'
' Render with:  plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/booking_sequence.puml
' =================================================================================================

skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor "End user" as User
participant "Client\n(CLI / UI)" as Client
participant "BookingService" as Service
participant "Catalog\n(immutable)" as Catalog

User -> Client : open app
Client -> Service : listMovies()
Service -> Catalog : movies()
Catalog --> Service : MovieInfo[]
Service --> Client : MovieInfo[]
Client --> User : show movie list

User -> Client : select a movie
Client -> Service : listTheatersForMovie(movieId)
Service -> Catalog : showings()
Catalog --> Service : ShowingInfo[]
Service --> Client : TheaterInfo[] (deduplicated)
Client --> User : show theater list

User -> Client : select a theater
Client -> Service : listSeats(movieId, theaterId)
Service -> Catalog : lookup showing
Service --> Client : SeatMap (e.g. a1..a20,\neach available or taken)
Client --> User : show seat map

User -> Client : pick seats a1, a2, a3
Client -> Service : bookSeats(showingId, {"a1","a2","a3"})

activate Service
note right of Service
  Single critical section, see
  concurrent_booking.puml for what
  happens when two clients race here.
end note
Service --> Client : BookingResult{Ok, bookingId}
deactivate Service

Client --> User : confirmation + booking id

@enduml
